dropped the body
--
GCC's __builtin_shuffle (a vector-extension builtin, no N5008 clause):
element i of __builtin_shuffle(v, mask) is v[mask[i] % N].  The C front
end models it (the same program as C verifies); the C++ front end reports
"symbol '__builtin_shuffle' is unknown".  cpp11_dropped_library_body_warning
uses exactly this call as its "unsupported construct" in a system header,
so it has to switch to a different construct when this is fixed.
Reference compilers: g++ 13 accepts it (clang has __builtin_shufflevector
instead and rejects it).  Found by the round-163c audit of descs that
expect a rejection or a drop.  Pre-existing (round-162 snapshot bin51).
